<title>NORWAY: Norsk Hydro sees uncertain metals markets.</title>
<headline>Norsk Hydro sees uncertain metals markets.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian industrial giant Norsk Hydro ASA said on Monday it expected demand for aluminium to increase in 1997.</p>
<p>But Norway's largest listed company said new industrial production capacity and the potential start up of idled capacity created uncertainty regarding the fundamental balance in the market.</p>
<p>In a statement announcing 1996 results, Hydro said the magnesium market was experiencing high inventories and some downward pressure on prices.</p>
<p>--Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
